From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ieee1905: Steering Policy is nine bytes per radio, and chirp reads inside the TLV

Two validator faults found while mapping the byte layout of every
operational TLV against captured traffic (2026-07-19, re-verified
2026-08-10):

1. The Steering Policy TLV (0x89) checker advanced 8 bytes per radio
   while the spec, our own builder and our own struct all carry 9:
   radio id (6) + steering policy (1) + channel utilization threshold
   (1) + RCPI steering threshold (1). The comment said "1 byte for
   thresholds" - there are two. A well-formed TLV with any radios left
   num_radio bytes unconsumed and was rejected. Latent today, because
   the Policy Config Request CMDU is not in the validated list - but
   the first interop partner whose messages we validate would have
   been cut off by our own reference code.

2. The DPP Chirp Value (0xD3) checker read data[0], data[1] and
   data[7] before checking that the TLV was long enough to contain
   them - an out-of-bounds read on a truncated TLV. The length
   semantics themselves are correct (1-octet hash length, per spec).

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
--- a/src/extensions/map/tlv_checker.c
+++ b/src/extensions/map/tlv_checker.c
@@ -472,9 +472,9 @@
 	/* Validate each policy -
 	 * Each policy is 6 bytes for radio +
 	 * 1 byte for steer_policy +
-	 * 1 byte for thresholds.
+	 * 2 bytes for thresholds: channel utilization and RCPI.
 	 */
-	expected_len = 8;
+	expected_len = 9;
 	for (i = 0; i < num_radio; i++) {
 		if (remaining_len < expected_len)
 			return -1;
@@ -1381,10 +1381,16 @@
 	size_t expected_length;
 	uint8_t hashlen;
 
 	expected_length = sizeof(struct tlv_dpp_chirp);
+	if (datalen < expected_length)
+		return -1;
+
 	if (!!(data[0] & DPP_CHIRP_ENROLLEE_MAC_PRESENT)) {
 		expected_length += 6;
+		if (datalen < expected_length)
+			return -1;
+
 		hashlen = data[7];
 	} else {
 		hashlen = data[1];
 	}
